        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "f20bb0c7-b894-5dc1-a8fa-c6997aaa31fb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Marge Simpson, Homer Simpson, Julie Kavner, Dan Castellaneta, Margaret Groening\n- Works: Good Night, The Tracey Ullman Show, The Simpsons 138th Episode Spectacular, The Simpsons Season 1 DVD set\n- Topics: character origins, voice actors, broadcast and DVD releases\n\nFacts:\n- Marge Simpson first appeared on television in The Tracey Ullman Show short \"Good Night\" on April 19, 1987.\n- Homer Simpson first appeared on television with his family in The Tracey Ullman Show short \"Good Night\" on April 19, 1987.\n- Julie Kavner voices Marge Simpson.\n- Dan Castellaneta voices Homer Simpson.\n- The character Marge Simpson was named after Margaret Groening, the mother of her creator.\n- The short \"Good Night\" was later aired in its entirety in \"The Simpsons 138th Episode Spectacular\".\n- The short \"Good Night\" was also included on The Simpsons Season 1 DVD set, making it one of the few Ullman shorts released on DVD.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
